From db7e38565113e88e8ce6de7f5d42f93571920ec4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:11:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): an awake owner's replica row yields to its
 stamped projects-tree row, so parked work paints grey waiting [daveey]

With the hub as the active gateway, this Mac's older chats entered the sidebar as hub-replica fallback rows, which
carry no activity stamps (kanban_*, outcome). The overview overlay lets merged rows beat the tree's own copies, so
the backend's stamped row (kanban_active = kanban_parked) lost to the stamp-less copy and the row painted no stripe.
mergeOfflineFallback now takes the projects-tree rows and uses an awake owner's tree row in place of its replica
copy; an asleep owner's cached row stays cached.
